I have a strong suspicion about why "Finalize Trail" is failing. For the trail to save and appear, your **Supabase database** must have the correct tables and security policies (RLS) set up. If the tables don't exist or permissions are blocked, the app will try to save, get a hidden error from the server, and stay stuck on the screen.

### 🛠️ Important: The Fix (Supabase Side)
You need to run this SQL in your **Supabase SQL Editor** to create the necessary infrastructure. Copy and paste the following:

```sql
-- 1. Create Tables
create table if not exists public.profiles (
  id uuid references auth.users on delete cascade primary key,
  username text unique,
  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

create table if not exists public.trails (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  name text not null,
  creator_id uuid references auth.users on delete cascade not null,
  starting_view jsonb,
  created_at timestamp with time zone default now(),
  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

create table if not exists public.questions (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  trail_id uuid references trails on delete cascade not null,
  image_url text not null,
  location jsonb not null,
  title text,
  position_order int not null,
  location_source text,
  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

-- 2. Enable Security (RLS)
alter table public.profiles enable row level security;
alter table public.trails enable row level security;
alter table public.questions enable row level security;

-- 3. Create Policies
create policy "Public profiles are viewable by everyone" on profiles for select using (true);
create policy "Users can insert their own profile" on profiles for insert with check (auth.uid() = id);
create policy "Users can update own profile" on profiles for update using (auth.uid() = id);

create policy "Anyone can view trails" on trails for select using (true);
create policy "Users can create trails" on trails for insert with check (auth.uid() = creator_id);
create policy "Users can update own trails" on trails for update using (auth.uid() = creator_id);
create policy "Users can delete own trails" on trails for delete using (auth.uid() = creator_id);

create policy "Anyone can view questions" on questions for select using (true);
create policy "Users can insert questions for their own trails" on questions for insert with check (
  exists (select 1 from trails where trails.id = questions.trail_id and trails.creator_id = auth.uid())
);
create policy "Users can delete their own questions" on questions for delete using (
  exists (select 1 from trails where trails.id = questions.trail_id and trails.creator_id = auth.uid())
);

-- 4. Storage Bucket
-- Ensure you have a PUBLIC bucket named 'trail-images' in the Supabase Storage tab.
```

---

### Specification of App Updates

1.  **Detailed Error Feedback (`useTrails.ts` & `App.tsx`)**:
    *   Modified `saveTrail` to return the specific error message from Supabase instead of just `null`.
    *   `App.tsx` will now display the exact error (e.g., "relation 'trails' does not exist" or "new row violates row-level security policy") in the alert so you know exactly what's wrong with the database.

2.  **Instant Marker Placement (`Map.tsx`)**:
    *   Refined the marker placement logic to be more precise even when the map is animating or the layout is shifting.

3.  **Local Image Buffering (`QuizCreator.tsx`)**:
    *   As requested, we now use the local compressed image data for the "Confirm Marker" screen. The heavy upload to Supabase only happens when you hit "Confirm Marker", making the "Take Photo -> Tag Spot" transition nearly instant.

