I understand the frustration. If the images are uploading but the tables are empty, it confirms that the **database security (RLS)** or **schema mismatch** is the bottleneck. The marker jump is a classic Leaflet initialization race condition.

### 🛠️ Step 1: The "Clean Slate" SQL
Run this in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. This will wipe everything and recreate it exactly as the app expects. 

**⚠️ WARNING:** This will delete all existing trails and profiles.

```sql
-- Wipe everything first
drop table if exists public.questions cascade;
drop table if exists public.trails cascade;
drop table if exists public.profiles cascade;

-- 1. Profiles (Linked to Auth)
create table public.profiles (
  id uuid references auth.users on delete cascade primary key,
  username text unique,
  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

-- 2. Trails
create table public.trails (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  name text not null,
  creator_id uuid references auth.users on delete cascade not null,
  starting_view jsonb,
  created_at timestamp with time zone default now(),
  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

-- 3. Questions (Spots)
create table public.questions (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  trail_id uuid references public.trails on delete cascade not null,
  image_url text not null,
  location jsonb not null,
  title text,
  position_order int not null,
  location_source text,
  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()
);

-- Enable RLS
alter table public.profiles enable row level security;
alter table public.trails enable row level security;
alter table public.questions enable row level security;

-- Policies (Simplified for maximum reliability)
create policy "Public profiles are viewable" on profiles for select using (true);
create policy "Users can manage own profile" on profiles for all using (auth.uid() = id);

create policy "Anyone can view trails" on trails for select using (true);
create policy "Users can manage own trails" on trails for all using (auth.uid() = creator_id);

create policy "Anyone can view questions" on questions for select using (true);
create policy "Users can manage own questions" on questions for all 
using (exists (select 1 from trails where trails.id = questions.trail_id and trails.creator_id = auth.uid()));
```

---

### Specification of App Updates

1.  **Map Fix (`Map.tsx`)**: 
    *   The marker jump happens because Leaflet captures the click coordinate relative to a container that hasn't finished its animation/layout.
    *   **The Fix**: I've added an `invalidateSize()` call immediately inside the `click` handler before processing the location. This forces Leaflet to re-anchor itself to the actual screen pixels exactly when you tap.

2.  **GPS Priority Fix (`QuizCreator.tsx`)**:
    *   Ensured that if a live GPS coordinate is available, it is the absolute first choice for the marker position when taking a photo.

3.  **Finalize Trail Debugging (`useTrails.ts`)**:
    *   Added `upsert` logic for profiles to ensure they exist before a trail is saved.
    *   Added explicit schema checks in the code to handle the specific data types Supabase/Postgres expects.

